# Security Rules

Follow these security practices to protect Mafia Arena from vulnerabilities.

## Secrets Management

### Never Hardcode Secrets

```typescript
// ❌ NEVER - hardcoded API key
const OPENAI_KEY = 'sk-abc123...';

// ❌ NEVER - in code comments
// API key: sk-abc123...

// ✅ Good - use environment variables
const apiKey = env.OPENAI_API_KEY;
```

### Never Log Secrets

```typescript
// ❌ Bad - logs sensitive data
console.log('Config:', { apiKey: env.OPENAI_API_KEY, ...config });
console.log('Request headers:', request.headers);

// ✅ Good - redact sensitive data
console.log('Config:', { ...config, apiKey: '[REDACTED]' });
console.log('Request received for game:', gameId);
```

### Wrangler Secrets

```bash
# Set secrets via CLI (never in wrangler.toml)
wrangler secret put OPENAI_API_KEY
wrangler secret put ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
wrangler secret put GOOGLE_AI_API_KEY

# List secrets (values hidden)
wrangler secret list
```

### Environment Separation

```toml
# wrangler.toml - different configs per environment

[env.development]
vars = { ENVIRONMENT = "development" }

[env.production]
vars = { ENVIRONMENT = "production" }
# Secrets are set separately per environment
```

## Input Validation

### Validate All User Input

```typescript
import { z } from 'zod';

// Define strict schemas
const GameConfigSchema = z.object({
  playerCount: z.number().int().min(3).max(15),
  mafiaCount: z.number().int().min(1).max(5),
  teams: z.array(z.object({
    modelId: z.string().regex(/^[a-z0-9-]+$/),  // Restrict characters
    team: z.enum(['mafia', 'town']),
    count: z.number().int().min(1),
  })).min(2),
  maxRounds: z.number().int().min(1).max(20).default(10),
});

// Validate before processing
export async function handleRunGames(request: Request): Promise<Response> {
  const body = await request.json();
  
  const result = GameConfigSchema.safeParse(body);
  if (!result.success) {
    return Response.json(
      { error: 'VALIDATION_ERROR', details: result.error.issues },
      { status: 400 }
    );
  }
  
  // Use validated data
  const config = result.data;
}
```

### Sanitize String Inputs

```typescript
// Sanitize user-provided strings
function sanitizeInput(input: string): string {
  return input
    .trim()
    .slice(0, 1000)  // Limit length
    .replace(/[<>]/g, '');  // Remove potentially dangerous chars
}

// For display in HTML
function escapeHtml(str: string): string {
  return str
    .replace(/&/g, '&amp;')
    .replace(/</g, '&lt;')
    .replace(/>/g, '&gt;')
    .replace(/"/g, '&quot;')
    .replace(/'/g, '&#039;');
}
```

## SQL Injection Prevention

### Always Use Parameterized Queries

```typescript
// ❌ NEVER - string interpolation (SQL injection!)
const result = await db.prepare(
  `SELECT * FROM games WHERE id = '${gameId}'`
).first();

// ❌ NEVER - template literals
const query = `SELECT * FROM users WHERE name = '${username}'`;

// ✅ Good - parameterized queries
const result = await db.prepare(
  'SELECT * FROM games WHERE id = ?'
).bind(gameId).first();

// ✅ Good - multiple parameters
const result = await db.prepare(`
  SELECT * FROM games 
  WHERE status = ? AND created_at > ?
  ORDER BY created_at DESC
  LIMIT ?
`).bind(status, timestamp, limit).all();
```

### Validate IDs and Parameters

```typescript
// Validate ID format before query
const UUID_REGEX = /^[a-f0-9-]{8,36}$/i;

function validateGameId(id: string): boolean {
  return UUID_REGEX.test(id);
}

async function getGame(id: string): Promise<Game | null> {
  if (!validateGameId(id)) {
    throw new Error('Invalid game ID format');
  }
  
  return db.prepare('SELECT * FROM games WHERE id = ?')
    .bind(id)
    .first();
}
```

## Rate Limiting

### Protect Expensive Endpoints

```typescript
const RATE_LIMITS = {
  // Game creation - expensive (AI calls)
  'POST /api/games/run': { maxRequests: 10, windowMs: 60_000 },
  
  // Read operations - more lenient
  'GET /api/games': { maxRequests: 100, windowMs: 60_000 },
  'GET /api/leaderboard': { maxRequests: 100, windowMs: 60_000 },
};

// Apply rate limiting
async function checkRateLimit(request: Request, env: Env): Promise<boolean> {
  const ip = request.headers.get('CF-Connecting-IP') || 'unknown';
  const endpoint = `${request.method} ${new URL(request.url).pathname}`;
  const limit = RATE_LIMITS[endpoint];
  
  if (!limit) return true;
  
  const key = `ratelimit:${ip}:${endpoint}`;
  const current = parseInt(await env.KV.get(key) || '0');
  
  if (current >= limit.maxRequests) {
    return false;
  }
  
  await env.KV.put(key, String(current + 1), {
    expirationTtl: Math.ceil(limit.windowMs / 1000),
  });
  
  return true;
}
```

### Cost Controls

```typescript
// Daily budget check
const DAILY_BUDGET_USD = 10.00;
const AVG_COST_PER_GAME = 0.05;

async function canRunGames(count: number, env: Env): Promise<boolean> {
  const today = new Date().toISOString().split('T')[0];
  const key = `budget:${today}`;
  
  const currentSpend = parseFloat(await env.KV.get(key) || '0');
  const projectedCost = count * AVG_COST_PER_GAME;
  
  if (currentSpend + projectedCost > DAILY_BUDGET_USD) {
    console.warn(`Budget limit reached: $${currentSpend} spent today`);
    return false;
  }
  
  return true;
}
```

## Authentication & Authorization

### Protect Admin Endpoints

```typescript
// Simple API key auth for admin endpoints
async function authenticateAdmin(request: Request, env: Env): Promise<boolean> {
  const authHeader = request.headers.get('Authorization');
  
  if (!authHeader?.startsWith('Bearer ')) {
    return false;
  }
  
  const token = authHeader.slice(7);
  
  // Constant-time comparison to prevent timing attacks
  return timingSafeEqual(token, env.ADMIN_API_KEY);
}

function timingSafeEqual(a: string, b: string): boolean {
  if (a.length !== b.length) return false;
  
  let result = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < a.length; i++) {
    result |= a.charCodeAt(i) ^ b.charCodeAt(i);
  }
  return result === 0;
}
```

## Content Security

### CORS Configuration

```typescript
function getCorsHeaders(origin: string | null): Record<string, string> {
  const allowedOrigins = [
    'https://mafia-arena.pages.dev',
    'http://localhost:4321',  // Dev only
  ];
  
  const headers: Record<string, string> = {
    'Access-Control-Allow-Methods': 'GET, POST, OPTIONS',
    'Access-Control-Allow-Headers': 'Content-Type, Authorization',
    'Access-Control-Max-Age': '86400',
  };
  
  if (origin && allowedOrigins.includes(origin)) {
    headers['Access-Control-Allow-Origin'] = origin;
  }
  
  return headers;
}
```

### Response Headers

```typescript
function securityHeaders(): Record<string, string> {
  return {
    'X-Content-Type-Options': 'nosniff',
    'X-Frame-Options': 'DENY',
    'X-XSS-Protection': '1; mode=block',
    'Referrer-Policy': 'strict-origin-when-cross-origin',
    'Content-Security-Policy': "default-src 'self'",
  };
}
```

## Error Information Leakage

### Don't Expose Internal Details

```typescript
// ❌ Bad - exposes internal info
catch (error) {
  return Response.json({
    error: error.message,
    stack: error.stack,
    query: sqlQuery,
  }, { status: 500 });
}

// ✅ Good - generic error, log details internally
catch (error) {
  console.error('Database error:', {
    message: error.message,
    stack: error.stack,
    gameId,
  });
  
  return Response.json({
    error: { code: 'INTERNAL_ERROR', message: 'An error occurred' }
  }, { status: 500 });
}
```

## Dependency Security

### Keep Dependencies Updated

```bash
# Check for vulnerabilities
pnpm audit

# Update dependencies
pnpm update

# Check for outdated packages
pnpm outdated
```

### Minimize Dependencies

Prefer built-in APIs over external packages when possible:

```typescript
// ✅ Use built-in crypto
const id = crypto.randomUUID();
const hash = await crypto.subtle.digest('SHA-256', data);

// ✅ Use built-in fetch
const response = await fetch(url);

// ✅ Use Web Crypto API
const encoder = new TextEncoder();
const data = encoder.encode(message);
```

## Security Checklist

Before deploying:

- [ ] No hardcoded secrets in code
- [ ] All secrets set via `wrangler secret`
- [ ] Input validation on all endpoints
- [ ] Parameterized queries for all D1 operations
- [ ] Rate limiting on expensive endpoints
- [ ] Admin endpoints require authentication
- [ ] Error responses don't leak internal details
- [ ] CORS properly configured
- [ ] Security headers set
- [ ] Dependencies audited
